# What check.sh must find at the sync commit in SKILL.md: each rule that
# breaks in a setup, with TLC's shortest path to it (the actions, after
# the initial state). Every rule not listed holds. A line goes only when
# the code it describes changed, with the reason in the same change.

# Finding 1. A second confirmed run can start while the first still runs.
# The window starts afresh while `residue remove --trash --yes` runs (a
# quit and a relaunch, which can leave residue running, or the last-resort
# "Try again", which draws App anew), or the dialog fails to draw while it
# shows Moving and its Close returns to the list. Either way the worktree
# still shows as can go, and nothing in the app or in src-tauri knows that
# a run is in flight. Each run still sends only the worktrees its own list
# showed, and residue checks each one again (SKILL.md, "Findings").
remove/reload OneRemovalAtATime: YouTick YouClickMove PlanLands YouConfirm Reload ScanLands YouTick YouClickMove PlanLands YouConfirm
remove/draw OneRemovalAtATime: YouTick YouClickMove PlanLands YouConfirm DrawFails YouCloseBrokenDialog YouClickMove PlanLands YouConfirm
